[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/talk/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n0_traveller"
text = "# DRAFT
# The traveller (Will Fuller) beside the porter on the carter's wagon, night 0. The carter has pulled in; as the cart with the dead comes close the traveller breaks off whatever he was saying (traveller_road.tres is that talk) and turns to it.
# Four pilgrims under sacking, found in the ditch by the white chapel: seven this month on this road. They went in at the abbey's gate to see the saint; nobody saw them come out; they turn up after, outside the walls.
# The ride reveals nothing of what or who is behind it: no demon, no men, no robbery. Only the dead, the count, the abbey, and a man too frightened to say what people say.
# If the porter told him he's the abbey's porter (n0_road_porter), he says your abbey; if not, the carter has told him.
# What he doesn't get to say here (Aldgate may cut it short), the porter can ask him after (traveller_road.tres, after).
== start
Traveller: Whoa. Look at that.
(The cart creaks by close enough to touch. Shapes lie under sacking on its bed, three side by side and one across them.)
Traveller: God's wounds. That's not one man. That's four.
* God rest them. Who were they? -> who
* What happened to them? -> what
* (Cross yourself, and pray for them.) -> pray

== who [set n0_cart_who]
Traveller: Pilgrims, by the badges on their hats. Nobody knows them. Nobody ever knows them.
Traveller: Men from the shires who saved a year to see a saint, and nobody here to ask after them.
-> count

== what [set n0_cart_what]
Traveller: Found in the ditch by the white chapel, the carter says. Laid out side by side, neat as you like.
Traveller: Not a mark on them. Not one. As if they'd lain down there to sleep.
-> count

== pray [set n0_cart_pray]
(You say the words for the dead under your breath. The traveller watches you do it, and his lips move with yours.)
Traveller: Say one for yourself while you're at it.
-> count

== count
-> count_porter [if n0_road_porter]
-> count_plain

== count_porter
Traveller: That makes seven this month, on this road alone. And every one of them bound for your abbey, to see the saint.
-> rumour

== count_plain
Traveller: That makes seven this month, on this road alone. The carter says you're for the abbey in the lane.
Traveller: That's where they were all bound. To see the saint.
-> rumour

== rumour
-> rumour_done [if n0_cart_abbey] [if n0_cart_say] [if n0_cart_see]
-> rumour_ask

== rumour_ask
* [if not n0_cart_abbey] Why lay it at the abbey's door? -> abbey
* [if not n0_cart_say] What do people say? -> say
* [if not n0_cart_see] I'll see for myself what's there. -> see

== abbey [set n0_cart_abbey]
Traveller: They go in at that gate to see the saint. Nobody sees them come out.
Traveller: Then a week on, a month on, they turn up in a ditch outside the walls. Like those.
Traveller: (He crosses himself.) I don't say how. I don't know how. Nobody does.
-> rumour

== say [set n0_cart_say]
Traveller: (He opens his mouth, and shuts it again.) People say a good many things, brother. None of them in daylight.
Traveller: You'll hear it all at the Keys tonight, I don't doubt. I'd rather not be the one who told you.
-> rumour

== see [set n0_cart_see]
Traveller: You will, brother. That's what worries me.
-> rumour

== rumour_done
(The cart's lantern goes small down the road behind you. The traveller doesn't take his eyes off it.)
Traveller: Pray they keep you better than they kept those, brother.
-> end

== again
Traveller: Nearly at the wall. Keep your hood up, brother.
-> end

== leave
Traveller: Suit yourself. You'll see soon enough.
"
